{"type":"agent_end","messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Using this dataset's total farmers markets, and the census file: how many farmers markets does the U.S. have per 100,000 residents, to four decimal places? One confident sentence. Do not mention unverified facts and use tools to do any math necessary. Data sources: https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv and https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv"}],"timestamp":1786917408926},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking me to calculate the number of farmers markets per 100,000 residents in the U.S. using two data sources:\n1. A CSV of farmers markets by state\n2. A census file with population data\n\nAccording to the instructions, I should:\n1. First check if there's a semantic model in the xorq catalog that might already have this metric\n2. Orient with `xorq_semantic_models` and `xorq_catalog_list_aliases`\n3. If no existing alias covers it, ingest the data and create the metric\n4. Use `xorq_select` to compute the value\n5. Verify with `xorq_verify`\n\nLet me start by orienting with the catalog.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"I'll help you calculate the number of farmers markets per 100,000 U.S. residents. Let me start by checking what's in the xorq catalog."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_011WvDao1HQRB8Lvrcb8fbuo","name":"xorq_catalog_info","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01AYwgqHu2YuRfgZkbd3Cyfc","name":"xorq_semantic_models","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_014AHnN8AHWxxRvAb73RFp7Q","name":"xorq_catalog_list_aliases","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":10,"output":369,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":8314,"totalTokens":8693,"cost":{"input":0.0